From 0c7601243158a71a20336af25addf74b3ddd008e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:01:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix recovery gaps and journal scan cost found in the
 2026-10-01 audit

- Thread create/status/delete recover() report FAILED operations as BLOCKED
  instead of silently skipping them (E-005).
- Inventory knows thread-delete-v1 and the THREAD_DELETE operation shape, and
  flags unknown history directories instead of ignoring them (E-005).
- convert() rejects pending-delete receipts and core operation journals with
  operational_state_requires_import_policy instead of archiving them and
  releasing reserved identities (E-006).
- Information write scans for pending work and reserved event ids no longer
  read and validate compact receipts in full; receipts are still checked by
  event_id (T-049). 120 create+compact: 10.19 s -> 2.09 s.

Tests run with a local stand-in for pytest (real pytest unavailable): new
file passes, five of seven new tests fail without the fixes. Not run on a VM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
